  "verbalization": "Ofloxacin is suggested to be associated with External Ear Disease through a chain of indications that involve Norfloxacin, a related antibiotic. The evidence indicates that Ofloxacin is linked to Cystitis and Typhoid Fever, both of which are associated with Norfloxacin and, in turn, with External Ear Disease. This suggests a potential pathway where Ofloxacin may indirectly contribute to the development of External Ear Disease via its effects on other conditions. The strength of the connection is supported by multiple paths, each linking Ofloxacin to a different condition that ultimately leads to External Ear Disease. The mechanism appears to involve the use of related antibiotics in the treatment of infections, which may have broader implications for the pathophysiology of the disease. The evidence does not provide direct evidence of a direct causal relationship between Ofloxacin and External Ear Disease, but rather a chain of indirect associations through other conditions.",
